Google Chrome AD Group Structure – Proposed Design

Objective

The objective of this design is to simplify Google Chrome application and policy management by reducing the number of assigned groups and maintaining a single group for Chrome deployment and configuration. This approach improves manageability, reduces assignment complexity, and provides a clear access control model.

⸻

Proposed Group Structure

Primary Assignment Group

APPL-D-GoogleChrome-Install-Available

This group will act as the primary group for:

* Google Chrome application assignment
* Google Chrome policy assignment
* User access management through nested groups

This ensures that Chrome deployment and policy application are managed through a single assignment group.

⸻

Permission Groups

PERM-D-Intune-Chrome-AuthorizedOnly

* This group will remain nested under APPL-D-GoogleChrome-Install-Available
* Used to control access for users authorized to install Google Chrome
* Provides flexibility for managing Chrome eligibility without modifying application assignments

PERM-D-Intune-Win-DeveloperUsers

* Members of this group will be moved under APPL-D-GoogleChrome-Install-Available
* Continues to provide Chrome access for developer users
* Simplifies the overall group structure by removing unnecessary intermediate assignments

⸻

Group Decommissioning

APPL-D-GoogleChrome

* Existing policy assignment group can be removed
* Functionality will be consolidated into APPL-D-GoogleChrome-Install-Available

APPL-D-GoogleChrome-Install-Required

* Can be decommissioned after any existing users are migrated or removed
* No longer required in the simplified design

⸻

Benefits of the Proposed Design

* Single group used for Chrome policy and application assignment
* Reduced administrative overhead
* Simplified troubleshooting and ownership
* Clear access management through nested permission groups
* Elimination of redundant deployment groups
* Easier long-term maintenance and governance
